description:
Two interface pieces:

```cpp
std::vector<std::string> wrapText(const std::string& text, int maxWidth, int charWidth);

class Menu
{
public:
    void add(const std::string& label, bool enabled = true);
    void move(int delta);                 // -1 up, +1 down: next enabled item, wrapping around
    void hover(int index);                // the mouse is over an item: select it if enabled
    int selected() const;                 // -1 if no item is enabled
    std::string line(int index) const;    // "> Label" when selected, "  Label" otherwise, "  (Label)" when disabled
};
```

**wrapText** splits on spaces into lines no wider than `maxWidth` pixels, each character being `charWidth` wide (a fixed-width font). Words are kept whole and separated by one space; a word wider than a line on its own is put on its own line anyway. Several spaces in a row count as one, and an empty text gives no lines.

**Menu**: the first enabled item added becomes selected. `move` skips disabled items and wraps from the last to the first and back; if no item is enabled it does nothing.

